&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Server Engineer (Performance)&lt;/strong&gt; to join a new truly unique multiplayer strategy game in Barcelona on a hybrid basis or remotely in the UK, Ireland, Portugal, and the rest of Spain. If you&#39;re open to working in any of these locations, there&#39;s no need to apply more than once. We&#39;ll discuss location preferences during the hiring process. We can support with visa sponsorship from any location. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We embrace AI-forward development practices and expect our engineers to be curious and pragmatic about how these tools can raise the bar.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are in the early stages of development on an ambitious, unannounced Strategy/MMO title, creating a team of talented and passionate game makers to join us on this exciting journey!&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a cross-functional agile team and be responsible for designing, developing, and evolving systems that &lt;strong&gt;validate and improve the performance, scalability, and reliability of backend services running on AWS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement performance and reliability strategies for our core backend systems, including &lt;strong&gt;defining service-level expectations &lt;/strong&gt;(latency, throughput, error rates) and validating them under realistic conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build frameworks and tooling to simulate real-world production scenarios,&lt;/strong&gt; including multi-service interactions, high concurrency, and network variability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain load, stress, and endurance testing systems, integrated into &lt;strong&gt;CI/CD pipelines to detect regressions before production&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analyze system behavior using metrics, logs, and distributed tracing&lt;/strong&gt;, identifying bottlenecks and driving improvements across services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define and drive the adoption of a comprehensive testing strategy across backend services&lt;/strong&gt;, including unit tests, integration tests (leveraging test containers), and clear guidelines for when and how each layer should be applied&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable a shift-left quality culture by building tooling, patterns, and best practices&lt;/strong&gt; that allow teams to detect regressions early&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate with feature teams&lt;/strong&gt; to improve system design, resilience, and scalability, acting as a force multiplier across backend engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI tools and agentic workflows in your daily work — from tech planning, code generation and review to exploring novel solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly experienced&lt;/strong&gt; as a software engineer working on backend systems, distributed systems (operating in the Public Cloud) , or other relevant areas with a strong passion for testing and performance testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional experience &lt;strong&gt;building and operating highly available, scalable backend systems&lt;/strong&gt;, such as MMO game servers, high-traffic services, or real-time applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience with Python&lt;/strong&gt; and its ecosystem, including familiarity with asynchronous programming, concurrency, and &lt;strong&gt;performance considerations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solid understanding of distributed systems&lt;/strong&gt;, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;service-to-service communication, including event driven architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;failure modes and resilience patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;stateful vs stateless architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
